body:
Adds `vector` field type to support semantic search, RAG, and similarity matching workflows. QueryAST extensions (`having`, `distinct`, `windowFunctions`) and other modern field types (`location`, `json`) already existed.

## Changes

- **FieldType enum**: Added `'vector'` type for embedding storage
- **VectorConfigSchema**: Configuration for dimensions (1-10K), distance metrics (cosine/euclidean/dotProduct/manhattan), normalization, and index types (hnsw/ivfflat/flat)
- **Field factory**: Added `Field.vector()` helper with sensible defaults
- **Tests**: 19 tests covering OpenAI (1536d), image (512d), and RAG (768d) use cases

## Example

```typescript
import { Field, Object } from '@objectstack/spec';

const Article = Object.define({
  name: 'article',
  fields: {
    title: Field.text({ name: 'title' }),
    content: Field.textarea({ name: 'content' }),

    // OpenAI text-embedding-ada-002 for semantic search
    embedding: Field.vector(1536, {
      name: 'embedding',
      vectorConfig: {
        distanceMetric: 'cosine',
        normalized: true,
        indexed: true,
        indexType: 'hnsw'
      }
    })
  }
});
```

Driver implementations can leverage existing capability flag `vectorSearch` (PostgreSQL/pgvector, MongoDB Atlas, Pinecone, etc.).

